 "limitations": [
  "The primary contrast measures a phase difference, not recovery (M3, measured). In EXP-002, A1 is disordered before the shock in every cell (mean phi_pre 0.097 to 0.229), and phi_pre A1 - A0 (-0.312 [-0.319, -0.304]) is nearly equal to Delta (-0.307 [-0.313, -0.302]). The shock's effect on phi_post is small next to the stationary order level of each arm, so the rejection of H0 says that A1 is less polarized than A0 at w_c = 0.5, not that it recovers worse. Limitation 11 is therefore realised, and EXP-003 does not remove it (Delta_S grows with w_c).",
  "The design cannot measure A1's recovery of order (M4). A1 is disordered before the shock in every cell, so it has little order to lose or regain. The exploratory change score near zero (0.004 [-0.004, 0.012]) removes the \"A1 recovers worse\" reading but cannot show equal recovery; the smaller early drop of A1 (-0.017 [-0.026, -0.008]) is a floor effect, not resilience.",
  "A1's steady state was not checked (M4, second review pass). Rule R-BI tested only A0. A1's phi_post is close to its phi_pre, which rules out fast drift, but slow coarsening after step 3000 is not excluded. The order gap is a pre-shock gap, not shown to be stationary.",
  "A0 is disordered before the shock in 10 of 18 cells of the frozen design, even after the lengthened burn-in (rule R-BI, t_d = 3000; m(4000) between 0.070 and 0.347). In those cells phi_post says little about recovery; they are kept in the pooled estimand and flagged.",
  "Post hoc exploratory checks (M4). The change-score, subset, matched-cell and early-response analyses (X1 to X5, results/exploratory/M4-sensitivity/) were chosen after the confirmatory results were seen. They use the frozen bootstrap settings and change no verdict, but they are not preregistered.",
  "Simulation only. Every outcome is a property of the simulated model. No claim of biological fidelity, robot performance or universal distributed-system guarantees (master prompt section 10, claims boundary).",
  "Two dimensions, constant speed, discrete synchronous updates. Results may not transfer to 3-D, variable-speed, asynchronous or continuous-time models.",
  "One disturbance type in the primary design (heading shock of half the agents). Other disturbances (noise bursts, predators, agent loss, communication dropout) are not tested in the confirmatory design.",
  "Parameter ranges. Conclusions hold within the tested grid of density, noise and radius; extrapolation is not supported.",
  "A2 is not a realistic controller. The centralized reference is an idealised global-broadcast ceiling without delay or bandwidth limits.",
  "Arm A1 is one parameterisation of separation and cohesion (zonal priority, fixed weights); EXP-003 tests a few alternatives, not the space of rules.",
  "Provenance flag on EXP-003 runs (M3). 134 of 160 S1 runs and all 320 S2 and S3 runs record git_dirty: true, caused by an uncommitted journal edit during the runs; no code, configuration or protocol differed from revision 075cf7c, and 6 flagged runs re-simulated from clean code were bit-identical (DL-013)."
 ],
